now crosses the runner seam again after evaluation (issuing the git integrity command through both a directly-instantiated `LocalRunner` and the injected `EvaluatorRunner`, able to veto the applied state) and the edits shift every cited anchor in `candidate.rs` (lines 343/547/552) and `source.rs` (1040/1299), so CRT-02.2's \"where each seam is crossed\" is now incomplete and its line citations stale.","topic_sha256":"16710f0ae2246555baded3a7f982a3710fe8f05654b4581cd68fc4d3853587b8","artefact_sha256":"a03c73359b359dcc0e5c5648eaadd042465f84da60944c9e5e096e48886627b7","prompt":{"path":".diagram-review/triage/2026-11-04T05-17-00-065Z-triage-96c6dfdd-6ecc-4a01-b514-88992a040d5c/crates%2F02-seams-and-what-implements-them.md.prompt.txt","sha256":"04b93674042b82f4d8b0d18a0c7de75c5a6db5cd6521bd12844de20200515972"}},{"artefact":".diagram-review/triage/2026-11-04T05-17-00-065Z-triage-96c6dfdd-6ecc-4a01-b514-88992a040d5c/crates%2F01-crate-dependency-dag-and-the-licence-boundary.md.reply.txt","topic":"crates/01-crate-dependency-dag-and-the-licence-boundary.md","yes":false,"reason":"The change only adds an external crates.io dependency (`ontomark-compile`) and a pinned version to `dream-core/Cargo.toml`; the topic's workspace-internal DAG (CLI→CORE/GATE, CORE→GATE/FF, GATE→PW/FF, cited at unchanged lines 17–18) and its mechanism-level licence-policy claims about `deny.toml`/CI remain accurate, since third-party deps were already outside the diagram's stated \"inside the workspace\" scope.","topic_sha256":"6177af76e70dee71aca53df8601ad2386f416b983e481fe08dda689330b49eef","artefact_sha256":"4e3e232e32912399bcc1db4c0a8038dc62ea960eee9d2d613bc436758345b6bc","prompt":{"path":".diagram-review/triage/2026-11-04T05-17-00-065Z-triage-96c6dfdd-6ecc-4a01-b514-88992a040d5c/crates%2F01-crate-dependency-dag-and-the-licence-boundary.md.prompt.txt","sha256":"674b8f9da75c1679186a540cafe97a6a0ac6f05f9c97e20ea7df75626d5bcd7c"}},{"artefact":".diagram-review/triage/2026-11-04T05-17-00-065Z-triage-96c